# Line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows; the deploy target is Amazon Linux. A shell
# script committed from a Windows checkout carries CRLF, and the kernel then
# reads the shebang as "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and fails on the server with:
#
#     bash: line 1: /tmp/release-chat.sh: cannot execute: required file not found
#
# deploy/bin/* is fetched from S3 and executed on the EC2, so it must be LF
# regardless of who commits it or how their git is configured.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
